The rain stops for a little while.
I go outside for a leisurely walk.
Walking along, I reach a Sunday street market.
This street is very bustling.
Five months ago, I didn't know anything about this market.
I stop at a fruit cart.
Very nice mangoes are arranged there.
There are some small mangoes in front and some big mangoes at the back.
I ask, "Dada, how much are these mangoes?"
That shopkeeper says, "Madam, these are local mangoes."
"These are one hundred rupees a kilo."
I point to the back and ask, "And those big mangoes?"
He says, "Those are Alphonso mangoes, four hundred rupees a dozen."
I look at both these mangoes.
The fragrance of these small mangoes is very sweet.
I say, "Dada, give me one kilo of these local mangoes."
That shopkeeper puts those mangoes in a bag and gives them to me.
I give him one hundred rupees.
Now I have fresh mangoes, and I start walking again.
